I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:06.107 --> 00:00:09.514
are going to solve all of
the world's major problems.

00:00:09.514 --> 00:00:12.156
So to help you on your
journey, today's message is

00:00:12.156 --> 00:00:14.887
Find Balance in Your Life.

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:16.667
Over to you, Jet Li.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:19.165
(rooster crowing)

00:00:19.165 --> 00:00:21.711
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:21.711 --> 00:00:24.285
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:24.285 --> 00:00:27.785
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:32.826
(gloomy music)

00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:52.051
(cars honking)

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.433
- I think balance is really important,

00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:53.158
but I think it looks different
for different people.

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:56.500
I think you need to understand
what is balance for you.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.344
As an example, I remember
listening to an audio series

00:01:59.344 --> 00:02:01.735
by Tony Robbins, and I love Tony Robbins,

00:02:01.735 --> 00:02:05.166
and he was going through,
"Write down your list of goals,

00:02:05.166 --> 00:02:07.947
"and talk about, if you want
to be a painter, write down,

00:02:07.947 --> 00:02:09.302
"I want to make this painting," or

00:02:09.302 --> 00:02:10.745
"I want to write this masterpiece."

00:02:10.745 --> 00:02:12.071
"I want to create this poem," or

00:02:12.071 --> 00:02:13.266
"I want to make this sculpture,"

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.344
and because he was so
excited and into it, like,

00:02:15.344 --> 00:02:16.617
"Yeah, I want to make a painting,"

00:02:16.617 --> 00:02:18.030
"I want to make a masterpiece."

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.446
"I want to create a sculpture,"

00:02:19.446 --> 00:02:21.334
and it started building
up my list of things that

00:02:21.334 --> 00:02:24.281
I want to do, kind of outside
of just a business world.

00:02:24.281 --> 00:02:26.812
And then when I looked at it, I realized,

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:29.214
I don't actually really
want to do those things,

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:32.149
and I got kind of
externally motivated by Tony

00:02:32.149 --> 00:02:33.948
in that moment, but it's not really

00:02:33.948 --> 00:02:35.830
what balance means to me.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.391
And so I think it's super important,

00:02:37.391 --> 00:02:39.485
not to just look at somebody else's life,

00:02:39.485 --> 00:02:41.694
but to do a regular audit.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.728
I think one of the most
important things that you can do

00:02:43.728 --> 00:02:47.066
as a human being, is do a
quarterly audit of your life,

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:48.577
and see where are you spending your time,

00:02:48.577 --> 00:02:50.389
and does it match to the goals

00:02:50.389 --> 00:02:51.592
that you're trying to accomplish.

00:02:51.592 --> 00:02:55.434
So if you're feeling like
you're working too hard,

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.633
then what are the other
activities that you're doing?

00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.227
How much time are you spending?

00:02:59.227 --> 00:03:00.527
And doing that quarterly audit,

00:03:00.527 --> 00:03:02.368
because your life will always change,

00:03:02.368 --> 00:03:04.514
and your goals and your
priorities will change.

00:03:04.514 --> 00:03:07.765
My schedule changes at least once a month,

00:03:07.765 --> 00:03:10.369
but in a major way,
probably once a quarter,

00:03:10.369 --> 00:03:12.504
where I need to adjust
my priorities based on

00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:14.618
how I'm evolving as a human being.

00:03:14.618 --> 00:03:16.107
Some things I just don't
care about anymore,

00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:17.162
and I'm still spending time on.

00:03:17.162 --> 00:03:18.370
So I need to eliminate those.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.199
Some things I need to
spend more time on that

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.443
I'm drawn towards, and so
I need to factor that in

00:03:22.443 --> 00:03:24.069
and put it in my calendar.

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:27.172
I can tell what your priorities are

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.650
by looking at your calendar.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:31.831
So if there's something that
you think is really important,

00:03:31.831 --> 00:03:33.264
if you're trying to find more balance,

00:03:33.264 --> 00:03:34.544
if you're trying to work harder,

00:03:34.544 --> 00:03:36.719
you want to make sure that
these priorities get done,

00:03:36.719 --> 00:03:39.759
schedule it into your calendar,
both the personal things

00:03:39.759 --> 00:03:42.623
and the business things, and stick to it.

00:03:42.623 --> 00:03:44.799
If you do that, then you'll
be able to build the life

00:03:44.799 --> 00:03:45.910
that you want to lead.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.135
So the question of the day today is,

00:03:47.135 --> 00:03:51.099
I'm curious, what does
balance look like for you?

00:03:51.099 --> 00:03:52.771
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:03:52.771 --> 00:03:53.976
super curious to find out.

00:03:53.976 --> 00:03:56.270
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Deej Martinez.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.801
Deej, thank you so much for picking up

00:03:57.801 --> 00:04:00.111
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:00.111 --> 00:04:01.939
It really really really means a lot to me,

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:03.931
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:03.931 --> 00:04:05.357
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:04:05.357 --> 00:04:06.564
I believe in you.

00:04:06.564 --> 00:04:08.597
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:04:08.597 --> 00:04:10.943
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:10.943 --> 00:04:13.259
Much love, and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:13.259 --> 00:04:16.034
for another shot of Entspresso.

