♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:04:25.044 --> 00:04:26.877
- It's complex, right?

00:04:28.429 --> 00:04:30.762
And it's deceiving at times.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.337
You know, because people
think the two equate.

00:04:34.337 --> 00:04:35.302
- [Interviewer] Yes.

00:04:35.302 --> 00:04:37.124
- You know, to each other, and they don't.

00:04:37.124 --> 00:04:38.898
- [Interviewer] You have a lot of money.

00:04:38.898 --> 00:04:40.114
- It's up, yeah.

00:04:40.114 --> 00:04:42.414
And I have a lot of
happiness, but that doesn't

00:04:42.414 --> 00:04:44.158
mean that the two equate to each other.

00:04:44.158 --> 00:04:45.221
- Has your happiness risen

00:04:45.221 --> 00:04:47.111
at the same amount as your bank account?

00:04:47.111 --> 00:04:50.206
- No, that's the thing, they don't.

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:51.279
- [Interviewer] They don't
equate, or they're not

00:04:51.279 --> 00:04:52.168
tied in any way, or.

00:04:52.168 --> 00:04:54.273
- They're not tied to each other.

00:04:54.273 --> 00:04:55.364
I mean, it allows you freedom,

00:04:55.364 --> 00:04:57.571
and it allows you to go
places where you can smile,

00:04:57.571 --> 00:04:59.382
and look at the sunset
and things like that.

00:04:59.382 --> 00:05:02.205
That's what you choose to
do, and you enjoy to do.

00:05:02.205 --> 00:05:04.228
But there are a lot of
people with tons of money

00:05:04.228 --> 00:05:06.746
who aren't happy because either they

00:05:06.746 --> 00:05:08.681
become a prisoner of their money,

00:05:08.681 --> 00:05:12.039
or they become so consumed
with getting money

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:15.994
that they don't allow time for happiness.

00:05:15.994 --> 00:05:17.655
Life is about balance, right?

00:05:17.655 --> 00:05:19.083
You have to have some type of balance.

00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:21.786
You have, like, time for work,

00:05:21.786 --> 00:05:22.918
and there's time for play.

00:05:22.918 --> 00:05:25.249
And if you don't allow
these two things to coexist,

00:05:25.249 --> 00:05:27.683
you have an imbalance of one or the other.

00:05:27.683 --> 00:05:29.766
- I got great advice from

00:05:30.623 --> 00:05:32.677
one of the people that
totally fascinates me is

00:05:32.677 --> 00:05:36.967
Bob Iger, he's the CEO of
the Walt Disney, ABC world.

00:05:36.967 --> 00:05:39.361
So his job is so weird to me,

00:05:39.361 --> 00:05:41.411
because he is in charge of everything from

00:05:41.411 --> 00:05:44.406
a Disney cruise, to George
Stephanopoulos ABC news.

00:05:44.406 --> 00:05:47.239
To like, a theme park, to Scandal.

00:05:48.215 --> 00:05:50.916
All of that falls into
the ABC/Disney family.

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:53.382
And I asked him, and it
was very helpful to me,

00:05:53.382 --> 00:05:54.929
I asked him a few months ago, like,

00:05:54.929 --> 00:05:58.044
"How do you decide what you're
going to work on in a day?"

00:05:58.044 --> 00:06:00.145
And he said something so valuable to me,

00:06:00.145 --> 00:06:01.170
so I want to share it with you guys.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:05.051
He said, 80% of his time,
he tries to think about,

00:06:05.051 --> 00:06:06.995
"Where can I have impact?

00:06:06.995 --> 00:06:10.326
"Where am I going to make a
difference in the day today?"

00:06:10.326 --> 00:06:13.086
So it may not usually be Disney cruises,

00:06:13.086 --> 00:06:14.926
but sometimes it needs to be,

00:06:14.926 --> 00:06:16.738
because the cruise business has been doing

00:06:16.738 --> 00:06:17.960
what the cruise business is doing.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:19.465
That's not quoting him, by the way.

00:06:19.465 --> 00:06:21.830
(laughing)

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.978
Sometimes it's a Broadway
show that's about to open,

00:06:23.978 --> 00:06:26.391
sometimes it's the ESPYS, because ESPN,

00:06:26.391 --> 00:06:27.854
that's where his focus needs to be.

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:30.965
So it's really about like,
"Where can I have impact today?"

00:06:30.965 --> 00:06:32.234
"Where am I needed?"

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:35.909
And the other 20% is,
"What brings me joy?"

00:06:35.909 --> 00:06:38.037
So there are certain movie projects that

00:06:38.037 --> 00:06:41.431
fall under the ABC/Disney
world, that bring him joy.

00:06:41.431 --> 00:06:44.888
Or certain shows, or certain,
an opening of a park.

00:06:44.888 --> 00:06:47.187
There are certain things that bring him.

00:06:47.187 --> 00:06:49.239
That just fill him up, that fall in

00:06:49.239 --> 00:06:51.155
his work responsibilities.

00:06:51.155 --> 00:06:54.438
And I just really have
tried to bring that with me

00:06:54.438 --> 00:06:57.770
because it's important for us to remember

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.503
the joy in what we do.

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:01.921
It's important to be
effective in our workplace,

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.797
but it's important to
cultivate the moments that just

00:07:04.797 --> 00:07:08.111
bring us joy, because
that's how we'll shine

00:07:08.111 --> 00:07:10.948
in our lives as professionals, you know?

00:07:10.948 --> 00:07:12.452
- How do you balance so much?

00:07:12.452 --> 00:07:14.313
How do you balance having
such a successful career,

00:07:14.313 --> 00:07:17.830
and maintaining your social
life, your family, all of that?

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:19.346
- Well, it's a different
kind of enjoying yourself

00:07:19.346 --> 00:07:20.245
when you get older.

00:07:20.245 --> 00:07:22.960
As a young girl, before I got married,

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.377
I owned property, I had cars,

00:07:26.272 --> 00:07:29.772
I lived a luxurious life in fabulous,

00:07:29.772 --> 00:07:32.022
like, I was a bachelorette.

00:07:34.702 --> 00:07:38.874
My dance card was full, I
had boyfriends, I had a life.

00:07:38.874 --> 00:07:41.347
But a career is not going
to keep you warm at night,

00:07:41.347 --> 00:07:44.220
and money is not the answer to happiness.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.082
You know, you create an
equal balance of everything.

00:07:48.082 --> 00:07:50.971
At least that's what I
say, if you ask Wendy.

00:07:50.971 --> 00:07:52.274
That's what I say.

00:07:52.274 --> 00:07:54.774
And I only know that because
that's what I live by.

